<title>UK: Fortune says trading in line, eyes sell-offs.</title>
<headline>Fortune says trading in line, eyes sell-offs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil trading and distribution company Fortune Oil Plc said on Wednesday that trading in the year to date was in line with expectations.</p>
<p>The company, which has oil-related operations and investments in Guangdong province in China, said it was making &quot;good progress&quot; but gave no details.</p>
<p>Fortune said it was in talks to sell its British onshore oil production business, East Midlands Oil &amp; Gas Ltd.</p>
<p>It was also aiming to sell its Fuo Duo liquefied petroleum gas business in China, Fortune said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
